-- title:
--   Lemma D.6 — conditional Hoeffding lemma
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ be an integrable real random variable and $Z$ a random variable on a probability space, such that
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb{E}[V \mid Z] = 0 .
--   $$
--
--   Suppose that for some measurable function $f$ and some constant $c \ge 0$,
--
--   $$
--   f(Z) \le V \le f(Z) + c .
--   $$
--
--   Then for every $t > 0$, almost surely,
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb{E}\big[e^{tV} \mid Z\big] \le e^{t^2 c^2 / 8} .
--   $$
--
--   This is the conditional version of Hoeffding's lemma (Lemma D.1): given $Z$, the variable $V$ is centred and confined to an interval of length $c$. It is the one-step estimate behind Azuma's inequality (Theorem D.7).
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathbb{E}[\cdot \mid Z]$ is the conditional expectation with respect to the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $Z$; (in)equalities between conditional expectations hold almost surely.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: V, Z random variables, f a function, E[V | Z] = 0 → V integrable, Z and f measurable; reason: the conditional expectation E[V | Z] and the random variable f(Z) are defined only then (Lean's conditional expectation of a non-integrable function is the junk value 0); no instance where the book's statement is meaningful is excluded
--   - encoding: E[· | Z] and its (in)equalities → conditional expectation with respect to σ(Z), equalities and inequalities almost surely; reason: standard meaning of conditional expectation
-- source:
--   Mohri, Rostamizadeh & Talwalkar, Foundations of Machine Learning, 2nd ed., MIT Press 2018, p. 441 (PDF p. 458), Appendix D §D.6, Lemma D.6, (D.10)–(D.11)

import Mathlib

namespace MohriFoML.OnlineToBatch

open MeasureTheory

/-- **Lemma D.6: conditional Hoeffding lemma.**
Mohri, Rostamizadeh & Talwalkar, Foundations of Machine Learning, 2nd ed., MIT Press 2018,
Appendix D, §D.6, p. 441 (PDF p. 458), Lemma D.6, inequalities (D.10)–(D.11).

Let `V` and `Z` be random variables with `E[V | Z] = 0`, and let `f` be a function and `c ≥ 0` a
constant with `f(Z) ≤ V ≤ f(Z) + c`. Then for all `t > 0`, `E[e^{tV} | Z] ≤ e^{t²c²/8}`.

**Formalization Note.** `E[· | Z]` is the conditional expectation `μ[· | σ(Z)]` with respect to
the σ-algebra `MeasurableSpace.comap Z mβ` generated by `Z`; equalities and inequalities of
conditional expectations hold almost surely. `V` is assumed integrable, `Z` and `f` measurable:
"`E[V | Z] = 0`" and "`f(Z)` is a random variable" are meaningless otherwise (Lean's conditional
expectation of a non-integrable function is the junk value `0`). The bounds (D.10) are assumed
at every point of the sample space. -/
theorem cond_hoeffding_lemma {Ω β : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] [mβ : MeasurableSpace β]
    {μ : Measure Ω} [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    (V : Ω → ℝ) (Z : Ω → β) (f : β → ℝ) (c : ℝ)
    (hZ : Measurable Z) (hf : Measurable f) (hV : Integrable V μ)
    (hcond : μ[V | MeasurableSpace.comap Z mβ] =ᵐ[μ] 0)
    (hc : 0 ≤ c)
    (hlow : ∀ ω, f (Z ω) ≤ V ω) (hup : ∀ ω, V ω ≤ f (Z ω) + c) :
    ∀ t : ℝ, 0 < t →
      μ[fun ω => Real.exp (t * V ω) | MeasurableSpace.comap Z mβ]
        ≤ᵐ[μ] fun _ => Real.exp (t ^ 2 * c ^ 2 / 8) := by sorry

end MohriFoML.OnlineToBatch
